    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d349">

                <pb facs="0750" n="728" sameAs="frus:frus1950v05/pg728"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">357.AC/2–750:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            United States Delegation to the Palestine Conciliation
                            Commission, at Geneva</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d349-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-02-07T19:00:00-05:00">February 7, 1950—7
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>198. Unpal 245. Following are Dept’s views on
                    compensation questions raised Paluns 330 and
                        331.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d349-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Dept memo of Sept 6<anchor n="3" xml:id="d349-f3"/> states that determination
                    claims not necessarily prerequisite negotiating preliminary lump sum payment.
                    Modified postion our Jan 3 memo<anchor n="4" xml:id="d349-f4"/> recommending
                    survey refugee property as first step based on assumption unwillingness Israel
                    negotiate pending broader settlement. Boisanger proposal therefore correct in
                    principle but Dept feels now not appropriate time attempt apply it.</p>
                <p>Dept agrees with position you have taken and approves idea establishing machinery
                    for further study of problem. However, in interest harmonious relations with
                    Boisanger, Dept believes wld be desirable not give him impression his suggestion
                    rejected by Dept or USDel. You shld make
                    further efforts persuade him agree USDel
                    position. Following additional arguments may be helpful: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Arabs wld react unfavorably to lump sum payment as this might seem
                            indicate PCC has given up hope
                            repatriation.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>If Israel agreed at all to pay lump sum, amount wld certainly not be
                            large enough to satisfy Arabs.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Not desirable risk creating another impasse so soon in new series
                                PCC meetings.</item>
                        <pb facs="0751" n="729" xml:id="pg729"/>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item>Reaction Arab public opinion to Israeli refusal might result serious
                            stiffening Arab position.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>Dept disagreement first sentence Palun 331 set
                    forth in Jan 3 memo. Fully agree compensation should not be linked reparation
                    claims.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d349-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d349-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram was repeated to the U.S. Delegation to the United Nations in New
                    York.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d349-f2" n="2" xml:id="d349-f2-content">
                <p>Dated January 28 and 31, neither printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d349-f3" n="3" xml:id="d349-f3-content">
